From: aibox v0.25.7 / track T2 (WorkItem BACK-20260509_1316-TallBear)
Subject: [PATCH] release-audit: add stale-test grep sweep (project-configurable)

Adds a fifth check `stale_layout_tests` to the upstream release-audit
skill. It greps test files for project-configured magic-string patterns
(layout names, slot labels, harness identifiers, hardcoded tmux indices)
so the audit catches tests that pass under the current shape but would
silently break when the project changes those magic strings.

Project-configurable: the patterns live in
`context/skills/processkit/release-audit/stale-test-patterns.toml` (loaded
if present). When the file is absent the check is a no-op INFO. This
keeps the upstream skill provider-neutral.

Provenance: WorkItem BACK-20260509_1316-TallBear (aibox v0.25.7 / track T2).
A working project-local prototype lives at
`scripts/release-audit-stale-tests.py` and
`scripts/release-audit-stale-tests.baseline` in the aibox repo; this
patch is the upstream-ward generalization. Apply via the proper
processkit-skill-update MCP path — do NOT commit directly into the
project's `context/skills/processkit/release-audit/` mirror (vendored
read-only).

NOTE: this is a propose-only diff; line offsets are approximate. The
parent should regenerate against the upstream skill HEAD when applying.

